oh  testing out the Apple watch Ultra on the  extremes  the water fountain  yeah  after using the Apple watch Ultra for  some time we have some questions and  some of these questions might be the  same questions you have if you do have  them let us know in the comment section  below we're also going to get a  triathlete to really take this watch  through its Paces but this is a really  good watch and a watch like this is  gonna bring up a lot of discussion some  we may agree with and some we may not  and some we hopefully Apple will watch  this video and go hey we didn't think of  that or hey we actually have an answer  for that and we can find out because  this watch is going to open up the doors  to a whole new Marketplace for a lot of  you out there in the Apple ecosystem  that you've never had before in this  particular way first and foremost let's  talk about this Apple watch Ultra this  will be the watch I think a lot of you  out there will be aiming to get you  might not be a triathlete you might not  be an Iron Man athlete you might not  hype to Mount Everest it doesn't matter  most people who buy a Rolex Submariner  or a Panerai submersible like myself  don't do deep sea diving we get these  watches because we love the design and  let's be honest over the past 8  iterations of the Apple watch they all  look the same they might have gone a  little bit larger but really nobody  knows what series Apple watch you wear  with the ultra  now they know  when you wear the ultra  it signifies that your air is serious  or you could be you're a person who  takes help seriously you're looking to  push yourself you're going to stand out  in the crowd  and some people just want to flex that  way let's be honest but  we're going to talk about some of the  features that I think a lot of you out  there who do use the watch for these  type of things are going to really  appreciate okay case in point for me  personally I own two Garmin watches the  Phoenix 5 and a Garmin Mark 