ed you're naturally going to  gravitate to pinching both buttons at  the same time will that cause a problem  later on down the road for athletes will  they have to be remind themselves just  press on the left side for the action  button and don't press on that right to  hold that the watch on my wrist it's  gonna be interesting you might not think  of these small things but these are  things that do come up when you use the  watch over time they make it very  interesting another thing I like the  digital Crown it's a little bit larger  easier to use with gloves so as a  cyclist who uses gloves when I ride even  a motorcyclist for that matter I can now  access the digital Crown without  worrying about it the size of the watch  is very important a lot of you out there  going is this watch really that big 49  millimeters so I want this side of this  large size of a watch and look I wear a  patternized submersible 44 millimeters I  wear a Rolex gmt2 it's around 40 to 42  millimeters this watch feels really good  on the wrist it's very lightweight  thanks to the uh Aerospace Titanium on  it it feels really really nice and the  straps are absolutely awesome but they  are not cheap 100 US dollars per straps  so invest wisely pick the right color  and the right material I would say for a  lot of you out there that want that  larger display because you're going to  get six rows of information versus Five  On series eight this will come in handy  even if you want to read an email it's  easier to read on this watch versus a  series 8. well let's talk about some of  the other things in this watch you have  new GPS system you have an L1 GPS and L5  GPS very similar to what on polar and on  Garmin on the higher end watches but  it's reliant on the Apple Maps only now  depending on what part of the world  you're at Apple Maps may be fantastic or  maybe subpar you do not have a choice to  use another map system so if you use  Google Maps or whatever Maps you want to  use you can't you're reliant on Apple  Maps only now in the future they're  going to be having a diving application  which you can go deep sea diving they'll  be working with a third party vendor for  that because Apple doesn't do deep sea  diving so you'll be able to use this as  a dive computer which is fantastic we're  not going to test that right now because  we don't have the app on it but we're  going to go more into the uh the Iron  Man kind of workout cycling running  swimming with our triathlete we'll let  you know how that goes but I think  there's also some other questions that  we have now crash detection same as  series 8 but why was crash detection  only tested for car crashes what about  motorcycles what about cyclists for that  matter they say well you have fall  detection  okay  but wouldn't crash detection be more  viable for motorcyclist who gets flown  off the bike versus somebody in a car  with multiple airbags who's kind of  enclosed and is probably relatively safe  I don't know it's a question I have also  temperature readout now we know that  they talk about temperature readings in  terms of ovulation Cycles now I don't  have an ovulation cycle it doesn't work  for me what I would love to have because  over the past two years all I've been  doing is taking my temperature  everywhere I go because of covet I would  love to have a watch that tells me my  body temperature if I'm not feeling so  well that as you see the temperature  raising that alerts me hey your  temperature is raising a little bit if  you want to get checked out we know this  is not going to be a medical device but  we have the ECG readings on this we have  the heart monitor readings on this we  have all these things that will alert us  when our heart rate goes up it'd be nice  to have this for our temperature at  least let me know if I want to check my  body temperature for whatever reason I  can check it it may not be 100 accurate  I get it but it would be nice to have  and of course for 